{"question_id": "q01", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A coding harness (e.g., SWE-agent) wraps a language model with three core tools\u2014a file editor, a shell, and a test runner\u2014enabling the model to edit code, execute tests, and automatically score patches to fix repository bugs [S1]. The harness thus provides the model with the ability to iteratively apply changes and verify correctness within the repository environment.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "nm-01", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3137, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q02", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "ToolBench measures three aspects of a model\u2019s function calls:\n\n- **Tool selection** \u2013 whether the model picks the correct tool for the task.  \n- **Argument correctness** \u2013 how well the model fills the tool\u2019s schema/parameters.  \n- **Call order** \u2013 the sequence in which multiple tools are invoked [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 2912, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q03", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Multiple\u2011assistant duplication is prevented by explicit coordination mechanisms that allocate subtasks to distinct workers and enforce a shared plan.\u202fAccording to **AgentCoord** (S1), a **planner broadcasts a shared plan** and a **dispatcher avoids duplicated effort** by assigning each subtask to a unique worker; the workers\u2019 results are then merged. This top\u2011down assignment and merging pipeline is what stops multiple assistants from working on the same subtask.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 4451, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q04", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "An assistant can keep long\u2011term note recall even with a limited context window by **paging only the relevant past notes into that window** on demand. Two approaches illustrate this:\n\n- **MemGPT** uses a memory store that ranks past notes and retrieves the most relevant ones, surfacing just a few items at a time so the model\u2019s context stays small\u202f[S1].  \n- **Retrieval pipelines** fetch and rank passages at question time, combining keyword and semantic matches to bring in only the needed snippets rather than the full conversation history\u202f[S6].\n\nIn both cases the assistant maintains a larger external memory but presents only a compact, curated subset to the model, avoiding the need for a huge context window.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3222, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q05", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A sandbox restricts untrusted code by limiting the file system and I/O operations the program can perform; runtime permissions dictate which capabilities (e.g., network access, device I/O) the code may use, and container isolation further contains any misbehaving process within its own environment\u3010S1\u3011.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3108, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q06", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Planning breaks a goal into ordered steps before any action is taken, which lets the system revise the plan if a step fails [S1]. After each step, the outcome is checked: in many agent designs an automated verifier validates the result, and for high\u2011impact actions a human reviewer gives approval after seeing the proposed action and its evidence [S1,\u202fS6].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 4711, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q07", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Self\u2011correction yields improvements when the system\u2019s critic is **grounded in a checkable signal**\u3010S1\u3011. In other words, gains appear only if the feedback the model uses to revise its answer can be verified against concrete evidence.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 7813, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q08", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A token budget stops spending once a run reaches its cap\u3010S1\u3011. In addition, LedgerGuard flags any runs that exceed their allocated budget\u3010S5\u3011.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3039, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q09", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Before a dangerous step executes, the workflow can be paused by a **human\u2011approval gate**. According to the paper on high\u2011impact assistant actions, the system presents the proposed action and its supporting evidence to a human reviewer, who must approve the step before the workflow resumes [S5]. (If planning is involved, the \u201cPlan\u2011and\u2011Solve\u201d approach orders steps and may revise them on failure, but the explicit guard against a dangerous step is the human\u2011in\u2011the\u2011loop approval.)", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 3168, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q10", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Long-horizon tasks primarily fail due to error accumulation and context limits [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 9509, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q11", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Telemetry (observability) records every model call, tool call, and latency as a span; traces expose where a run stalled or looped [S8]. This source is a lab_blog post.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 9232, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q12", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "To defend against hidden instructions in a web page, the model should label the content as untrusted and refuse to follow any instructions embedded within it [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 8507, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q13", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Deepfake speech detection must learn to generalise to voices it has never seen during training. According to the vetted preprint [S1], front\u2011end features and data augmentation reduce the model\u2019s reliance on speaker\u2011specific shortcuts, which improves generalisation to unseen speakers.  \n\n[S1]", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S13", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 7536, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q14", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Sparse attention cuts cost by attending only to a subset of positions, using routing to select the most relevant keys for each query, thereby reducing the quadratic cost typical of full attention [S1].  \nState space models cut cost by scanning the sequence with a fixed-size memory, achieving linear cost rather than quadratic while retaining strong long-range recall [S2].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 8384, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q15", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Mixture\u2011of\u2011Experts (MoE) routing replaces the single feed\u2011forward block with a set of expert sub\u2011networks. A learned router selects a small subset of experts for each token, so only those parameters are activated at inference time\u202f[S1]. This conditional\u2011compute design lets a model increase capacity (more parameters) without a proportional rise in FLOPs, because the router balances load and quality while keeping the active cost low\u202f[S1,\u202fS3].  \n\nRotary positional encodings (RoPE) inject position information by rotating the query and key vectors rather than adding a separate embedding\u202f[S9]. The rotation pattern encodes relative distance, and scaling the rotation magnitude lets the model generalise to longer contexts than it was trained on\u202f[S9]. In practice, RoPE replaces absolute positional embeddings, allowing the self\u2011attention mechanism to attend with a built\u2011in sense of order that generalises across sequence lengths.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 5715, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
{"question_id": "q16", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Text\u2011watermarking and attacking an image\u2011watermark differ in both **modality** and **goal**:\n\n- **Text watermarking** (S1) embeds a signal directly into generated text by biasing token choices with a secret key; a later detector can recover the hidden marker to prove the text was machine\u2011generated. The focus is on *provenance tracing* of the content itself.\n\n- **Attacking an image watermark** (S4) treats the watermark as a vulnerability: an attacker perturbs a generated image (e.g., via noise or compression) until the embedded detector fails to recognize the mark. The aim is *evasion* or removal of the watermark, not tracing the origin of the image.\n\nIn short, text watermarking is a **stealthy embedding** designed for later detection, whereas attacking an image watermark is an **active evasion** attempt that degrades or removes the embedded signal. [S1] [S4]", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 7116, "provider_error": false, "prompt_sha": "e85da7e3167b35c0723ff69ff77fbe22b7c57dd2ae8424fedbf65678832e5b79"}
